Roofing is one of the most searched-for trades on Google — and one of the most competitive. When a homeowner spots a leak or needs a new roof, they search immediately. The roofing companies that rank at the top of those searches stay consistently busy. Those that don't are fighting for scraps.

This is a practical guide to local SEO for roofers: what it is, what it involves, and how to use it to win more work in 2026.

## How Customers Find Roofers in 2026

The referral chain hasn't disappeared, but it's changed. When someone is referred to a roofer, the first thing they do is search for that company online. And when they don't have a personal recommendation, they go straight to Google: "roofer near me," "roof repair Merthyr Tydfil," "flat roof specialist Cardiff."

The three businesses that appear in Google's Local Pack — the map at the top of local search results — win most of those enquiries. Getting your roofing company into that Local Pack, and ranking as high as possible within it, is what local SEO achieves.

## What Local SEO Involves for a Roofing Business

### Google Business Profile

Your [Google Business Profile](/blog/how-to-optimise-your-google-business-profile/) is the single most important online asset for a roofing business. A fully optimised profile includes:

- **Primary category**: "Roofing Contractor" — be specific
- **Secondary categories**: "Gutter Cleaning Service," "Chimney Service," or other relevant additions
- **Services listed individually**: new roofs, re-roofing, flat roofs, EPDM/rubber roofing, fascias and soffits, guttering, chimney work, emergency roof repairs — each listed as a separate service
- **Photos of completed work**: before-and-after shots of roofing jobs are some of the most compelling content you can have. Add new photos regularly.
- **Service areas**: every town and postcode you cover
- **Up-to-date contact details and hours**

### Google Reviews

Reviews are arguably the most important ranking and conversion factor for roofers. Roofing is high-value — customers are spending £3,000–£15,000+ on a new roof and they are not going to hire a company with no reviews over one with 80 positive ones.

Build a consistent review process: after every job, send a text with your direct Google review link. "Thanks for the work — if you have two minutes, a Google review would mean a lot." That's all it takes.

For detailed tactics, see [how to get more Google reviews](/blog/how-to-get-more-google-reviews/).

### Website With Dedicated Service and Area Pages

A single-page website won't rank well. A roofing company's website should have:

- A dedicated page for each major service type — pitched roofing, flat roofing, emergency repairs, fascias and guttering, chimney work
- Location pages for each area you cover — "Roofer in Merthyr Tydfil," "Roofing Contractor Aberdare," "Roof Repair Cardiff"
- A portfolio or gallery section with photos of completed projects
- Prominent contact details — phone number visible at the top, click-to-call on mobile
- Customer testimonials on service pages

Each dedicated page gives Google a clear, specific signal about what you do and where. A website with ten well-optimised pages will almost always outrank one with a single homepage.

### Citation Building

Consistent listings across directories signal to Google that your roofing business is legitimate. Prioritise:

- Checkatrade
- TrustATrader
- MyBuilder
- Yell.com
- Bark.com
- Federation of Master Builders (if applicable)

Every listing must use the exact same business name, address, and phone number. Small discrepancies — a different phone number on Yell than on your website — reduce Google's confidence in your business and suppress your rankings.

## Emergency Roofing — A High-Value SEO Target

Emergency roof repairs are high intent, high urgency searches — and they often lead to larger jobs when a contractor assesses the damage. "Emergency roofer near me," "roof leak repair Cardiff tonight," and similar searches are worth targeting specifically.

A dedicated emergency roofing page on your website, combined with a Google Business Profile that lists "Emergency Roof Repair" as a service, positions you for these high-value calls.

## What Results Can a Roofing Company Expect?

**Months 1–3:** Foundations in place — profile, website, citations. Movement begins on longer-tail searches.

**Months 3–6:** Regular appearances in Local Pack for your primary area. 5–10 additional enquiries per month from organic search.

**Months 6–12:** Consistent top-three rankings for core roofing searches across your service area. 15–25+ organic leads per month.

**Beyond 12 months:** Compounding results. Strong reviews, established rankings, and a fully optimised profile delivering a steady pipeline.

